  },
  "listen_face": {
    "about": "The face of the one listening on its nods (eyes.md, 'План: брови по тону и лицо слушающего', item 3): now and then a nod as the other one speaks comes with a flash of the brows smaller and shorter than the flash cue (its weights times weight, its times times time); a friendly listener smiles a little instead (S_FRIENDLY times smile.weight, smile.chance) or smiles and flashes (smile.flash); an angry or hostile one frowns a moment instead (the frown cue made smaller and shorter), never smiles or flashes. A face on about one nod in two or three (chance) and at most once in gap_ms. Limits picked by the clip, the look is the user's.",
    "chance": 0.45,
    "gap_ms": 4000,
    "flash": {
      "cue": "flash",
      "weight": 0.6,
      "time": 0.8
    },
    "frown": {
      "cue": "frown",
      "weight": 0.6,
      "time": 0.45
    },
    "smile": {
      "weight": 0.5,
      "on_ms": 400,
      "hold_ms": 700,
      "off_ms": 600,
      "chance": 0.6,
      "flash": 0.3
    }
  },
  "speech_face": {
    "about": "The face from the voice (engine-plan.md, step 10) on a head with Mark's shapes (face-shapes.md, 'Формы Mark в игре'): a track of Audio2Face v3.0 weights, solved for Mark's shapes, plays as it is but for mouthClose x1.4 (our lips are fuller than Mark's: where Mark shuts them, Vino's stayed 1.0-1.3 mm apart in 6 % of the frames of the clip, 1 % with it; the lip over the upper one unchanged) - no cap; eyeLook* dropped (the gaze is Eyes'). The track's eyeBlink* is the level of the lids, the blinks go over it. A track made with an emotion has the expression: the mood faces of the line give way to it while it shows and come back after it.",
    "fade_in_ms": 80,
    "fade_out_ms": 250,
    "scale": {
      "mouthClose": 1.4
    },
    "drop": [
      "eyeLook*"
    ],
    "mood_faces": [
      "S_FRIENDLY",
      "S_ANGRY",
      "S_HOSTILE",
      "S_FRIGHTENED",
      "T_HURT"
    ]
  }
